--
N5008 [class.copy.elis]/[stmt.return]/2 -- returning a local by value
used to relocate the object BITWISE through the return-value mechanism
(three hops), breaking a move constructor that branches on the source's
self-pointer state (the SSO shape; std::string by value read a dead
object).  Fixed by the elide_cpp_returned_temporaries lowering: the
callee constructs the result directly into caller storage via a hidden
result pointer (guaranteed copy elision, as compilers implement it),
with [class.copy.elis]/3 implicit move at the return site.
Header-free, 14 essential lines; g++/clang++ runtime-verified.
